3.45.m:
One desiring a son obtains a son; one desiring a daughter obtains a daughter;
one desiring knowledge obtains knowledge; and one desiring offspring obtains offspring.
One who has lost his kingdom regains his kingdom; one who has lost his wealth regains wealth. // 68

4.2.m:
Hearing Rādhikā's words, some cowherd maidens were seized with fear;
all of them, with folded hands and necks bowed in devotion,
standing before that chaste, beloved one, all spoke to her: // 36
